      "text": "General Contractor & Roofing Longmont CO | Josh Brooks Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. is a licensed general contractor in Longmont, Colorado, founded in 2014. Owner Josh Brooks has 30 years in construction. We run every job start to finish as your GC. We don't take subcontract work for other GCs or owner-managed ('self-GC') jobs. Every project needs a deposit to schedule and begin — no exceptions. Not ready for a deposit? Please contact another contractor. 📞 Call (720) 828-7997 | 💬 Text Photos of Damage: (720) 453-5095 Get a Free Estimate → Skip to content Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. Home Project Videos Services Roofing James Hardie Siding Basement Finishing Kitchen & Bath Remodeling Window Replacement Decks & Additions Veteran & Senior Discounts Service Areas Longmont Boulder Erie Fort Collins Greeley Loveland Aurora Denver Metro Firestone Brighton Thornton Westminster Commerce City Berthoud Golden Our Process Gallery Blog About Contact Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. Home Project Videos Services Roofing James Hardie Siding Basement Finishing Kitchen & Bath Remodeling Window Replacement Decks & Additions Veteran & Senior Discounts Service Areas Longmont Boulder Erie Fort Collins Greeley Loveland Aurora Denver Metro Firestone Brighton Thornton Westminster Commerce City Berthoud Golden Our Process Gallery Blog About Contact LICENSED CLASS C GENERAL CONTRACTOR | FULLY INSURED | CON-24-0152 Longmont’s Licensed General Contractor for Roofing, Remodeling & Hail Restoration Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. (also known as Josh Brooks Construction ) is an American general contractor and roofing company headquartered in Longmont, Colorado. Founded in 2014 by Josh Brooks, who has worked in construction since 1996, the company provides roofing, siding, windows, doors, decks, remodeling, and hail damage restoration in 46+ cities along the Colorado Front Range, from Fort Collins to Castle Rock. The company holds a Boulder County contractor license (CON-24-0152, Class C), a Jefferson County Class C license, and a Douglas County Class A license. Its stated policy is “Licensed. Local. Not a storm chaser.” It is not affiliated with similarly named “Brooks Construction” businesses outside Colorado. Josh runs every job himself. We work in five Front Range counties. We are local. We are not storm chasers. 📞 Call Josh: (720) 828-7997 💬 Text a Photo of Your Damage ⚡ Get an Accurate Estimate Same-day storm help. A written quote in 24 hours. Free checks, no pressure. see exactly what to expect ✓ 30 Years in Construction ✓ Fully Insured $1M/$2M ✓ Boulder County CON-24-0152 ★ Veteran & Senior Discounts ★★★★★ 4.5 Star Average | Google • Houzz • Angi Direct Answer Who is Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. and what do they do? Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. is a licensed general contractor in Longmont, Colorado. Our license is CON-24-0152. We started in 2014. Josh Brooks, the owner, has worked in building since 1996. That is 30 years. We do roofing , siding, basements, and kitchen and bath work. We also build decks, put in new windows, and help with hail damage claims . It is all under one license. ✓ On-Site Owner Supervision: You deal with Josh from start to finish. ✓ Storm & Insurance Help: We meet your adjuster. Your hail claim stays simple. ✓ Quality Work: From taking out walls to new Pella windows. Why Choose Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc.? We have worked on Front Range homes since 2014. Josh has 30 years in the trade. He runs every job himself. That goes for roofs, siding, remodels, and hail repair. He works with your adjuster from the first look to the last walk-through. You can see each step of our process before you call. Want the back story? Read about Josh and the company . “Licensed. Local. Not a storm chaser.” — Josh Brooks, owner, Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. The Brooks 60-Second Roof Check Does Your Roof Need Attention? The Brooks 60-Second Roof Check is our own homeowner checklist, built from what we look for first on every Front Range roof inspection. Tap anything you’ve noticed at your house and see what it usually means and what to do next. You find shingle granules in your gutters, or see bare or bruised spots on the shingles. That usually means the shingles are wearing out or took hail hits. We’ll inspect it for free and photograph what we find, so you have proof if it turns into an insurance claim. Call 720-828-7997 or text 720-453-5095 . Your home went through a hailstorm in the last year. Get it looked at before you call your insurance company. We tell you honestly whether there’s real damage, and we document it for the claim if there is. Most policies set a deadline for filing, so check yours. Call 720-828-7997 or text 720-453-5095 . You have a water stain on a ceiling or wall. Most leaks start at flashing, vents, valleys or a cracked pipe boot, not in the middle of the roof. We find the actual source and fix that, instead of just patching the stain. Call 720-828-7997 or text 720-453-5095 . Shingles are lifting, creased or missing after a windstorm. Fix those soon. Once a shingle lets go, water and wind get under the next row and into the roof deck. We handle repairs like this all the time, including ridge caps and decking. Call 720-828-7997 or text 720-453-5095 . Your roof is 15 or more years old. Colorado sun and hail age asphalt shingles fast. Start planning now. We only install Class 4 impact-resistant shingles, and many insurers give a discount for them. Call 720-828-7997 or text 720-453-5095 . None of these. Good news. Give the roof a quick look from the ground after every big storm, and keep our number handy for when something changes. Call 720-828-7997 or text 720-453-5095 . Start Here How Do You Get a New Roof in Colorado? A Quick Guide This page starts simple and goes deeper. Read it all, or jump to what you need: The basics: when to get your roof checked Our 2026 roofing prices What the experts say Sources and references Step 1: The basics Hail hits the Front Range hard. A hit roof can look fine and still leak months later. So get it checked soon after a big storm. Is your roof more than 20 years old? Then it is more likely to fail. The numbers below show why. Step 2: What it costs Once you know you need a roof, you want the price. Our real 2026 price per square is in the price table below . It builds on step 1 above. Step 3: Going deeper Want the fine print? See what the experts say about Class 4 shingles further down. Then read our full Colorado roof cost guide and our roofing and insurance FAQ . No Surprises — Here’s How It Works 1 Free Inspection We check, photo, and note it all, roof to base. It is free. You owe us nothing. 2 Scope & Materials You get a written plan with real product picks. For a hail claim, we work with your adjuster. 3 Written Price. Locked. You sign before work starts. The price you OK is the price you pay. 4 Build & Walkthrough Josh runs the work on site. Then he walks the job with you before you pay the rest. See the full step-by-step process → Real Work. Real Results. Recent Jobs: Which One Looks Like Your House? These are our own crews and our own photos from Front Range jobs. If one looks like what you’re dealing with, call and tell us which one. Thornton, CO · Roofing Hail-damaged roof replaced with Class 4 shingles After a 2-inch hailstorm, we tore off the damaged roof and installed Owens Corning Duration STORM Class 4 shingles in Estate Gray, with new synthetic underlayment, step flashing around the dormer, and new vents. Need the same? Call 720-828-7997 Before After Erie, CO · Kitchen Remodel Granite out, white quartz in This homeowner wanted a brighter kitchen. We replaced the granite on the island, the cooktop wall and the butler’s pantry with white quartz. The before and after photos are from the same island. Need the same? Call 720-828-7997 Longmont, CO · Bathroom Remodel Soaking tub and walk-in shower A full gut and rebuild: Durock cement board and waterproofing first, then marble-look porcelain, a tiled soaking tub with lit niches, and a walk-in shower with a pebble floor. Need the same? Call 720-828-7997 Before After Longmont, CO · Porch Tile porch rebuilt in Trex composite The old tile front porch was coming apart. We demoed it and rebuilt the surface in Trex composite decking, which won’t crack in freeze-thaw like tile does. Same porch, before and after. Need the same? Call 720-828-7997 Berthoud, CO · Siding James Hardie siding over brick We installed James Hardie fiber cement lap siding on the gable ends above the original brick, with new soffit, fascia and gable vents. We’re an authorized James Hardie installer. Need the same? Call 720-828-7997 Left Hand Canyon · Roof Repair Wind-damaged roof repaired around solar High canyon winds tore off ridge caps and exposed the decking. We pulled the solar panels, repaired the decking and ridge, and reinstalled the panels. Need the same? Call 720-828-7997 Data You Can Trust Why Shouldn’t Colorado Homeowners Wait on Home Repairs? The numbers tell the story. According to NOAA, Colorado gets some of the worst hail in the country. Waiting on repairs most often costs you more. 38 hail storms of a billion dollars or more hit Colorado from 1980 to 2024 According to NOAA NCEI $1.9B in damage from one Denver hail storm in May 2024. It was the second worst in state history. According to NOAA NCEI 3× more likely to file a hail claim if your roof is 20 or more years old Source: Insurance Industry Data 96% of the cost comes back when you sell after a small kitchen redo. Few home jobs pay back more. According to the 2025 Cost vs. Value Report As Josh Brooks, the owner, puts it: “I’ve been doing this in Northern Colorado since 2014. I’ve seen one hail storm take a roof from fine to failing overnight. Most people don’t notice until months later, when the leak shows up. So get your roof checked within 30 days of a storm. It’s the best thing you can do to protect your claim and your home.” — Josh Brooks , owner, Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. Licensed general contractor. License CON-24-0152. 30 years in the trade. Our Own Data How Much Does a New Roof Cost in 2026? Our Prices (First-Party Data) This is our own data, from our own 2026 price sheet. It is not a US average. It is not copied from some other site. You won’t find these numbers anywhere else, because they are our prices. As noted in step 2 above, this is what you pay us per square. Every roof we build follows one rule. We call it the Josh Brooks Class 4 Standard™ . It is our own proprietary installation method, built from 30 years of Colorado roofs. It has two parts: Every shingle roof gets Class 4 shingles. These are the top grade for hail. We use Owens Corning Duration STORM or better. We don’t put on standard shingles at all. Every roof gets all new metal and flashing. We don’t reuse old parts. Why Class 4? It stands up to hail better. Many insurance firms also give you a discount for it. See how Class 4 shingles can lower your premium . Josh Brooks Construction 2026 installed price per roofing square (our data) Roof system Our price per square Class 4 impact-resistant shingles (with all new metals and flashing) $1,000 Metal roofing $1,200 Concrete tile $2,000 Roof coating $1,000 A square is 100 square feet of roof. So a 25-square roof in Class 4 shingles runs about $25,000 with us. Your final price depends on your roof. We set it after we look. Want the full breakdown? Read our 2026 Colorado roof replacement cost guide . Next, see what the experts say below . Going Deeper Are Hail-Resistant Roofs Worth It? What the Experts Say This part builds on our price data above. Here is what outside experts say. Underwriters Laboratories (UL) According to UL, Class 4 is the top hail grade a roof can get. The test is called UL 2218. A 2-inch steel ball is dropped on the same spot twice. A Class 4 shingle must not crack. Insurance Institute for Business & Home Safety (IBHS) According to IBHS expert Dr. Ian Giammanco, PhD, managing director of atmospheric science at IBHS, Colorado makes up only about 10% of the national market for impact-resistant shingles, even though the state sits in Hail Alley. IBHS fires lab-made hail at full-size roofs at its research center in South Carolina. In a 2025 study, Giammanco and fellow IBHS researchers found that small hail under 1 inch, which the National Weather Service doesn’t even rate as severe, slowly wears shingles down. Weathered shingles that took small-hail hits were about ten times more likely to be damaged by a later large hailstorm. Impact-resistant shingles held their granules only slightly better under repeated small hail, so every roof should get checked after a hail season, not just after the big storms. It took about eight years of fieldwork to understand all the properties of hail. We replicate that in our laboratory and then we go test the products. — Dr. Ian Giammanco, PhD , managing director of atmospheric science at the Insurance Institute for Business & Home Safety, speaking to KOAA News , December 9, 2025 Rocky Mountain Insurance Association Insurance expert Carole Walker, executive director of the Rocky Mountain Insurance Association, told KOAA News in December 2025 that in Colorado, “many of the insurers give a discount for having hail resistant roofing products.” Ask your insurer what discount applies before you choose a shingle. And when we’re getting a re-roof, we’re asking that roofer, telling them these are the products that we want. — Carole Walker , executive director of the Rocky Mountain Insurance Association, speaking to KOAA News , December 9, 2025 Colorado Division of Insurance The Colorado Division of Insurance says to get a written quote and check a roofer’s past work before you hire. This is key after a storm. Josh Brooks, licensed general contractor “Every roof I put on gets Class 4 shingles and all new metals and flashing,” says Josh Brooks, owner of Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. “That’s our standard. No exceptions.” Still have a question? Check the roofing and insurance FAQ , or call Josh at 720-828-7997 . All sources are listed at the bottom of this page . General Contractor in Longmont, CO Josh Brooks Construction and Renovation Inc. is a licensed general contractor in Longmont, CO , with 30 years in construction. We are the building contractor Longmont homeowners call when a project needs more than one trade: framing, drywall, plumbing and electrical coordination, finishes, roofing, siding and windows, all under one contract with one point of contact. Home Remodeling in Longmont Our home remodeling in Longmont covers kitchens and bathrooms , basement finishing , decks and additions and whole-home remodels. As a remodeling contractor in Longmont , we plan the work in the right order so you are not paying two trades to undo each other. Why Hire One Building Contractor Instead of Several Trades? One contract means one schedule, one permit holder and one person accountable for the result. We hold Boulder County license CON-24-0152, and the owner stays on the job from estimate to final walk-through. Call 720-828-7997 or text 720-453-5095 for a free estimate. What Services Do We Offer? Every Trade, One Call From the roof to the basement, we do it all. ☀ Roofing & Insurance Claims We know Colorado hail. We note every inch of damage. We meet your adjuster and push for a full new roof. Learn More → 🏘 James Hardie Siding We are a James Hardie Elite installer. It comes with a 30-year warranty. It stands up to hail well. Insurance often pays for it. Learn More → 🏛 Remodeling & Additions Kitchens, baths, basements, and home additions. We pull the permits. One crew. One contract. Learn More → 🍁 Decks, Patio Covers & New Construction Our patio covers turn heads. We also handle deck installation and deck repair in Longmont with Trex, plus pergolas, and 